<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gotthard Kettler</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1517–1587</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gotthard Kettler was the last Master of the Livonian Order. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonian-war">Livonian War</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> invading, he placed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonia">Livonia</a> under Poland-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> by the Union of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vilnius">Vilnius</a> in 1561 and secularised the order. In return he became the first Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/courland">Courland</a> and Semigallia, a Polish-Lithuanian fief, and governor of Livonia, and introduced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lutheranism">Lutheranism</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gotthard-kettler.jpg" alt="Gotthard Kettler" width="320" height="372" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gothards_Ketlers_(16th_c).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
